      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 20-1143, Badgerow versus Walters."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Counsel, we have said or suggested from time to time that the FAA doesn't provide federal question jurisdiction. So how do you square that with the notion that Section 4, Section 8, provide such jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Daniel L. Geyser",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 16,
        "start": 16
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Section 9 is a ministerial function of confirming the award. You don't even need to know generally what the underlying dispute was about, whether it's a federal question or otherwise."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Geyser",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just to give an example, for the 12-month period that ended in March of 2020, there were 332,000 civil filings in U.S. district courts nationwide. So far this year, in the AAA alone, they've adjudicated 380,000 arbitrations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: -- that's not their -- that's an amicus argument. That's not their argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: But wouldn't you -- to pick up on Justice Breyer's questions, doesn't it make sense to have a -- a uniform rule if you're not going to have, oh, the Act itself confers jurisdiction, a uniform way to think about jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chamber of Commerce",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "first section of that Act. And this is a little bit of what the -- the Chamber of Commerce was arguing in their brief, but that is to say the first question just says go file in any court without regard -- any motion in federal court, but then it takes away and says but only if you have jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, what do we do with Section 8?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Petitioner says there are two ways for him to win. One is that Section 4 is a free-standing jurisdictional grant, contrary to what this Court has said in three separate Supreme Court cases."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2021-20-1143",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4cd0802427d56c590292fa45df9e87034aab9d0edcd6baeb3ed1f664dd59d4fb",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4cd0802427d5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. GEYSER: Thank you, Your Honor. A few quick points. First, starting with the venue argument, my friend said that Cortez Byrd called Section 4 a venue provision. That's simply false."
    },
    {
